meta {
  name: Events - Create
  type: http
  seq: 187
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/spaces/<cuid of an events space>/events
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Weekly review office hour",
    "body": "Bring your questions about the weekly review.",
    "starts_at": "2026-11-18T17:00:00+01:00",
    "ends_at": "2026-11-18T18:00:00+01:00",
    "time_zone": "Europe/Brussels",
    "meeting_url": "https://meet.example.com/abc-defg-hij",
    "location_visibility": "members",
    "capacity": 40,
    "replay_expected": true,
    "state": "draft"
  }
}

docs {
  Creates an event (#1513): a draft by default. The posting policy of the space decides who can create one. The times are ISO 8601 with the offset of time_zone at that time; the server stores the UTC instants. A published event with a start in the future tells the members at Everything after 5 minutes (notify_now: true skips the wait, for the moderators of the space). In a public space, anyone on the internet can read a published event, never its address or its place. capacity (1 to 5 000, or null) is the limit of places: it counts the Yes answers of the members who can read the space. With a token, the answer holds capacity only with the ability event-answers:read. replay_expected true offers the answer "Replay only". location_visibility going gives the address and the place to the members who answer Yes, the host, the owner and the admins (#1515). Ability events:write.
}
